1. Add Playlist References
==========================

In an org-mode file, add a ‘#+YOUTUBE-GT_UPDATE:’ directive with a
playlist URL or channel URL:

   *Playlist URL:*

     * My Playlist

     #+YOUTUBE-GT_UPDATE: https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLPdNX2arS9MYUGoIp0qogtHZ3fXu46GQt

   *Channel URL (all uploads):*

     * Channel Videos

     #+YOUTUBE-GT_UPDATE: https://www.youtube.com/@mynameisandong/videos

   This fetches all uploaded videos from the channel's uploads playlist.

   *Optional: use offset parameter to skip videos*

   Skip the first N videos from a playlist using the ‘:offset=N’
parameter:

     * Show only recent videos (skip first 100)

     #+YOUTUBE-GT_UPDATE: https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLPdNX2arS9MYUGoIp0qogtHZ3fXu46GQt:offset=100

   This skips the first 100 videos and displays only videos 100 onwards.
The index column starts from the offset value (100 in this example).


File: youtube-gt.info,  Node: 2 Generate/Update Tables,  Next: 3 Add Manual Notes,  Prev: 1 Add Playlist References,  Up: Usage

2. Generate/Update Tables
=========================

Run the update command:

     M-x youtube-gt-update-all

   This generates a table below the directive:

     #+YOUTUBE-GT_UPDATE: https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLPdNX2arS9MYUGoIp0qogtHZ3fXu46GQt
     | 0  |  |  |  7:13 | 2024-01-15 | [[https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=TOg98tz6ZZM][TOg98tz6ZZM]] | Video Title Here |
     | 1  |  |  | 12:45 | 2024-01-20 | [[https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=abc123][abc123]]          | Another Video    |


File: youtube-gt.info,  Node: 3 Add Manual Notes,  Next: 4 Update Behavior,  Prev: 2 Generate/Update Tables,  Up: Usage

3. Add Manual Notes
===================

The second and third columns are reserved for manual notes:

     | 0  | watched | important |  7:13 | 2024-01-15 | [[...][...]] | Video Title |
     | 1  |         | to-review | 12:45 | 2024-01-20 | [[...][...]] | Another Video |

   These notes are *preserved* on the next ‘youtube-gt-update-all’ run.


File: youtube-gt.info,  Node: 4 Update Behavior,  Prev: 3 Add Manual Notes,  Up: Usage

4. Update Behavior
==================

   • New videos are added with sequential indices
   • Existing videos retain their manual notes
   • Videos removed from the playlist are marked with index "NA" but
     kept in the table
   • Video metadata (title, date, duration) is refreshed


File: youtube-gt.info,  Node: Table Format,  Next: Configuration,  Prev: Usage,  Up: Top

Table Format
************

Column   Description                                        Example
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1        Video index (0-based) or "NA" for removed videos   ‘0’, ‘1’, ‘NA’
2        Manual note column 1                               ‘watched’
3        Manual note column 2                               ‘important’
4        Video duration                                     ‘7:13’, ‘1:23:45’
5        Publication date (ISO format)                      ‘2024-01-15’
6        Video URL (org link with video ID as label)        ‘[[https://...][abc123]]’
7        Video title                                        ‘Video Title Here’


